        "question": "Is workplace electric vehicle charging considered a taxable Benefit-in-Kind?",
        "answer": "No. Under HMRC regulations, electricity provided at an employer's business premises for employees to charge their electric cars is completely exempt from Benefit-in-Kind tax, regardless of whether the vehicle is a company car or the employee's personal vehicle."
