        "question": "How are plug-in hybrid electric vehicles (PHEVs) taxed under HMRC BiK rules?",
        "answer": "Plug-in hybrids with CO2 emissions between 1 and 50g/km are taxed based on their electric-only zero-emission range. Vehicles capable of driving 130 miles or more on pure electric battery pay only 2% to 3% BiK, while those with less than 30 miles electric range face significantly higher BiK rates of up to 14%."
